Ladybird now gives a range input with “appearance: none” a track
with no band whose height wraps its thumb, and centers the thumb of a
native slider on the band by its own height. Blink and WebKit lay out
the slider the same way: Their UA style sheets make
::-webkit-slider-container a flex box, and
::-webkit-slider-runnable-track a centered block (align-self: center)
with an automatic block size. So an unstyled track wraps the thumb and
centers it, and an author who sizes the track positions the thumb
with its margin. Gecko instead always centers the thumb in the
range’s content box, in nsRangeFrame::DoUpdateThumbPosition().
